-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ב/3 (6.12.2021), השלמת שעות עבודה על ידי מורים השוהים
-- בבידוד עקב חזרתם מחו"ל.
-- A teaching employee isolated after private travel abroad gets no
-- isolation or sick pay and may not teach remotely; for isolation on the
-- dates the circular names, the lost hours may instead be made up on free
-- days by 4.3.2022, and hours not made up are absence without pay.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time in this file is counted in DAYS from 7 December 2021 (day 0), the
-- first isolation date the circular names. The dates it prints, as days:
`7 December 2021`  MEANS 0
`9 December 2021`  MEANS 2
`14 December 2021` MEANS 7
`4 March 2022`     MEANS 87

§ `תשפ"ב/3 השלמת שעות עבודה על ידי מורים השוהים בבידוד עקב חזרתם מחו"ל`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 The letterhead, the date and the reference number; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13 The circular's number, the addressees (the owners and the school principals), the greeting and the subject line; no rule.

@desc The designation of the country a teaching employee returned from, as the circular names it ('מדינות כתומות', 'מדינות אדומות'); the designation itself is made outside the circular.
DECLARE `country designation` IS ONE OF
    `an orange country`
    `a red country`
    `a country of another designation`

@desc One day a teaching employee spent in isolation, with the working hours the isolation cost that day.
DECLARE `isolation day` HAS
    `isolation date`        IS A NUMBER  @desc the day, counted in days from 7 December 2021
    `working hours missed`  IS A NUMBER  @desc the hours of the employee's assignment that day that were not worked because of the isolation

@desc A teaching employee in isolation on returning from abroad, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `isolated teaching employee` HAS
    `returned from private travel abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
    `designation of the country left`     IS A `country designation`
    `days in isolation`                   IS A LIST OF `isolation day`

@desc One occasion on which a teaching employee works hours to make up the hours isolation cost.
DECLARE `make-up session` HAS
    `make-up date`                                    IS A NUMBER  @desc the day of the session, counted in days from 7 December 2021
    `hours worked in the session`                     IS A NUMBER
    `on a free day under the original assignment`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc a day free to the employee at the institution under the original assignment for the school year תשפ"ב
    `coordinated with the principal or the owner`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc coordinated with the school principal or the owner's authorised official
    `the employee consents`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `overtime under the Hours of Work and Rest Law`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc the hours would be overtime within the meaning of the Hours of Work and Rest Law, 5711-1951

§§ `Isolation pay and remote teaching`

-- The circular restates the Economic Assistance Program (Novel Coronavirus)
-- (Temporary Provision) Law, 5780-2020: it decides only the private-travel case.
@ref akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law denies isolation pay and sick pay for the isolation days` e IF
    e's `returned from private travel abroad`

-- ¶14 says a teaching employee also cannot teach remotely on isolation days;
-- ¶17 makes it a prohibition on the employee who has returned from abroad
-- into isolation. The text sets no time limit, so the prohibition has none.
@ref akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `isolation action`
DECIDE `no remote teaching from isolation` e IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `work from home or teach remotely`
    LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "תשפ\"ב/3: a teaching employee in isolation after returning from abroad may not work from home or teach remotely"

DECLARE `isolation action` IS ONE OF
    `work from home or teach remotely`
    `make up the missed hours` HAS `hours made up` IS A NUMBER
    `treat hours as absence without pay` HAS `hours treated as unpaid` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Making up the hours`

-- ¶15: the isolation dates whose hours may be made up, by designation.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15
GIVEN d IS A `country designation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular opens a make-up window for` d IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `an orange country` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a red country` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A `country designation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `last isolation date of the window` d IS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `an orange country` THEN `9 December 2021`
    WHEN `a red country` THEN `14 December 2021`
    OTHERWISE `7 December 2021` MINUS 1

GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`, i IS AN `isolation day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hours of this isolation day may be made up` e i IF
        e's `returned from private travel abroad`
    AND `the circular opens a make-up window for` (e's `designation of the country left`)
    AND i's `isolation date` AT LEAST `7 December 2021`
    AND i's `isolation date` AT MOST `last isolation date of the window` (e's `designation of the country left`)

GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours that may be made up` e IS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `working hours missed`)
             (filter (GIVEN i YIELD `the hours of this isolation day may be made up` e i)
                     (e's `days in isolation`)))

-- ¶15's conditions on a session: a free day under the original
-- assignment, coordinated with the principal or the owner's authorised
-- official, with the employee's consent, by 4.3.2022, and no overtime.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15
GIVEN s IS A `make-up session`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the session counts as making up` s IF
        s's `on a free day under the original assignment`
    AND s's `coordinated with the principal or the owner`
    AND s's `the employee consents`
    AND s's `make-up date` AT MOST `4 March 2022`
    AND (NOT s's `overtime under the Hours of Work and Rest Law`)

GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`, sessions IS A LIST OF `make-up session`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours made up` e sessions IS
    min (`hours that may be made up` e)
        (sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `hours worked in the session`)
                  (filter (GIVEN s YIELD `the session counts as making up` s) sessions)))

-- ¶16: making up the hours replaces deducting them; ¶18: what is not made
-- up is absence without pay. Hours outside the window cannot be made up, and
-- the law (¶14) pays nothing for them, so they are unpaid as well.
@ref akn:hc_1/p16 akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`, sessions IS A LIST OF `make-up session`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours of absence without pay` e sessions IS
    `hours missed in isolation` e MINUS `hours made up` e sessions

GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours missed in isolation` e IS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `working hours missed`) (e's `days in isolation`))

@ref akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN e IS AN `isolated teaching employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `isolation action`
DECIDE `making up the isolation hours` e IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `make up the missed hours` h
          PROVIDED h AT LEAST `hours that may be made up` e
    WITHIN `4 March 2022`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  PARTY `the employer`
          MAY   `treat hours as absence without pay` u
                PROVIDED u AT MOST `hours that may be made up` e

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: the signatures of the two officials and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- The hours are placeholders: the circular sets none.
`a teacher back from a red country` MEANS
    `isolated teaching employee` WITH
        `returned from private travel abroad` IS TRUE
        `designation of the country left`     IS `a red country`
        `days in isolation`                   IS LIST `isolation day` 0 6, `isolation day` 3 6, `isolation day` 7 6, `isolation day` 8 6

`a teacher back from an orange country` MEANS
    `isolated teaching employee` WITH
        `returned from private travel abroad` IS TRUE
        `designation of the country left`     IS `an orange country`
        `days in isolation`                   IS LIST `isolation day` 0 5, `isolation day` 2 5, `isolation day` 3 5

`a valid session of 12 hours` MEANS `make-up session` 40 12 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a session after the deadline`  MEANS `make-up session` 90 12 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a session in overtime`         MEANS `make-up session` 40 12 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- Red: 7.12–14.12 can be made up (days 0, 3, 7); day 8 (15.12) cannot.
#ASSERT `hours that may be made up` `a teacher back from a red country` EQUALS 18
-- Orange: only 7.12–9.12 (days 0 and 2).
#ASSERT `hours that may be made up` `a teacher back from an orange country` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `hours of absence without pay` `a teacher back from a red country` (LIST `a valid session of 12 hours`) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `hours of absence without pay` `a teacher back from a red country` (LIST `a session after the deadline`, `a session in overtime`) EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `hours made up` `a teacher back from an orange country` (LIST `a valid session of 12 hours`) EQUALS 10

#TRACE `making up the isolation hours` `a teacher back from a red country` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `make up the missed hours` 18 AT 40
#TRACE `making up the isolation hours` `a teacher back from a red country` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `treat hours as absence without pay` 18 AT 95
#TRACE `no remote teaching from isolation` `a teacher back from a red country` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `work from home or teach remotely` AT 3
